Phase 2 item 6 (second half) — streamed tool output + paginated OutputRef
==========================================================================
Node: M2.7 (Basic Prompt Compiler and one-agent runtime)
Item: Future-tasks.md Phase 2 item 6, second half (§2.4 defect)
Revision: commit "Phase 2.6: streamed tool output as run events +
paginated OutputRef" (amended to carry this file), phase2/loop-hardening
Environment: macOS darwin 25.5.0 arm64, local dev profile, UTC

WHAT CHANGED (audit class before: NOT-FOUND for streaming; the runtime
output_refs table had ZERO callers)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
shell.run captured output fully and tailed 8KB inline — no progress
during execution, no pagination.

- domain: ToolOutputChunk run event (broker_run_id, offset,
  byte_length, bounded preview <=256 chars).
- event-store: EventStore holds the RuntimeStore on the SAME db file —
  the runtime tables are wired into production for the first time;
  read_output_range gives clamped ranges with the true total.
- scheduler: ToolOutputSink flows through the registry boundary. The
  production sink shares run-plane state with the EventStoreObserver
  (sequence accounting + current-run cell under one lock), so lifecycle
  events and chunk events interleave on one consistent Run aggregate.
- run_streaming_capture: drains offset-addressed broker output every
  25ms while the process runs (chunk event per drain), final-drains
  after exit, stores the full bytes as a content-addressed OutputRef
  (outref-<broker_run_id>). Cancellation and timeout semantics are
  unchanged from Phase 2.3 (kill the broker run, no orphan process).
- shell.run result: 2KB inline tail + output_ref {output_ref_id,
  byte_length, preview}.
- surface: ReadOutputRef RPC — offset/max ranges, server-clamped 512KB
  pages, opaque ids (primary keys; no path surface). TS bindings
  regenerated in the same commit. docs/21 updated.

